  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner D13 / T244 keyless rule">
      The account sets `disableLocalAuth: true` and `customSubDomainName` (Entra needs it). No `listKeys()` anywhere and no
      key output. CustomerStampKeylessTemplateTests must cover it (raise the CognitiveServices local-auth count to 3).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">
      The stamp UAMI gets Cognitive Services User (a97b65f3-24c7-4388-baec-2e87135dc908) scoped to the account,
      principalType ServicePrincipal, skipped when the principal id is empty — same shape as doc-intelligence.bicep.
      Cognitive Services OpenAI User does NOT cover Content Safety dataActions.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="region">
      Prompt Shields + groundedness are regional. Add `contentSafetyLocation` to customer.bicep defaulting to `location`
      (the stamp default is westus2, which the module documents as supported); do not hard-code a second region.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">
      No live Azure change in this task (T186 deploys a stamp; T230 makes the real MI call). Do not change dev, demo or
      shared-prod resources or settings. Keep `ContentSafetyAuthHandler`'s key branch (local dev may paste a key) — only the
      stamp manifest and template lose the key.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10 / ADR-032">
      The boot check follows CacheModule: required outside Development and Testing (throw InvalidOperationException naming
      `AiSafety:ContentSafety:Endpoint`); in Development/Testing an unset endpoint registers the client with no base address
      so scans fail open through the services' existing catch (no new service, no new package). Registrations stay
      unconditional. Measure publish size against a fresh master build from short paths and run the CVE check.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="manifest discipline">
      Regenerate the catalog outputs with Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 (never hand-edit `generated/*`); run its -Verify.
      Remove the `ContentSafety-ApiKey→T246` pin; the known/pinned gap lists only shrink.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Any stamp or L2 component other than the BFF's two safety services needs a Content Safety key or endpoint → STOP and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>`kind: ContentSafety` cannot take `disableLocalAuth: true` + custom subdomain at the pinned API version, even after raising it → STOP and report options.</trigger>
    <trigger>A BFF test host or deployed environment other than demo would fail the new boot check → STOP and report before changing its config.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Module: content-safety.bicep keyless (disableLocalAuth true, custom subdomain), `userAssignedIdentityPrincipalId` param + Cognitive Services User assignment, drop the `contentSafetyKey` output and the stale comment; refresh the header.</step>
    <step order="2">customer.bicep: naming var `sprk-{customer}-{env}-contentsafety`, `contentSafetyLocation` param, module call with the UAMI principal, `AiSafety__ContentSafety__Endpoint` in bffApi appSettings, LOAD-BEARING output `contentSafetyEndpoint`; recompile customer.json.</step>
    <step order="3">L2: BicepDeployOutputs.ContentSafetyEndpoint (required) + MapOutputs + H2a Check + InterStepState.ContentSafetyEndpoint + PerEnvSourceCatalog `from-h2a-output:content_safety_endpoint` + generator allowed list + HandlerRunInputs H4b input; fix every test that builds BicepDeployOutputs.</step>
    <step order="4">Manifest: per_env_settings `AiSafety__ContentSafety__Endpoint` (from-h2a-output:content_safety_endpoint, required); remove `ContentSafety-ApiKey` (comment like the T243 DocIntel removal); reword the MI literal's note; regenerate + -Verify; update RunContextContractTests (pin, positive control, RunSecretsReaders comment) and any manifest/H4b test naming the key.</step>
    <step order="5">BFF: AiSafetyModule boot check (constraint BFF §10); unit tests for Production-unset throws, Testing-unset boots, set endpoint used; template/Development template + ContentSafetyAuthHandler comments corrected (stamps have a ContentSafety account; the dev template endpoint is spaarke-openai-dev).</step>
    <step order="6">Verify-ContentSafetyResource.ps1: Entra token (`az account get-access-token --resource https://cognitiveservices.azure.com`) instead of the key; drop the Key Vault key-sync step.</step>
    <step order="7">Docs: resource inventory (Content Safety row), customer deployment guide, provisioning.md keyless list, AI docs that cite the fallback; plan G26/T246; T242c POML note (demo must set the endpoint); CHANGELOG.</step>
    <step order="8">Verify (bicep build + lint, customer.json = fresh compile, bicep-e2e-dry-run PASS, ControlPlane.Tests, ArchTests, BFF unit tests, publish size + CVE) + Step 9.5 + close + commit + push.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="file-modified">modules/content-safety.bicep; customer.bicep + customer.json; ControlPlane BicepInfraDeploy/Models/BulkAppSettings/Reconciler files + tests; manifest.yaml + generated/*; RunContextContractTests; AiSafetyModule.cs + BFF tests + appsettings templates + ContentSafetyAuthHandler comment; CustomerStampKeylessTemplateTests; Verify-ContentSafetyResource.ps1; docs; plan; T242c POML</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Compiled customer.json has a `Microsoft.CognitiveServices/accounts` resource of kind ContentSafety with `disableLocalAuth: true` and a custom subdomain, a Cognitive Services User assignment for the stamp UAMI on it, the `AiSafety__ContentSafety__Endpoint` app setting and the `contentSafetyEndpoint` output; no `listKeys` anywhere.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H2a maps `contentSafetyEndpoint` into InterStepState and fails when it is missing; H4b resolves `from-h2a-output:content_safety_endpoint`; the manifest has no `ContentSafety-ApiKey` and PinnedManifestGaps no longer lists it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git grep -n "spaarke-contentsafety-dev" -- src` returns nothing; the BFF throws at startup outside Development/Testing when the endpoint is unset (negative test) and boots in Testing without it (positive test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">CustomerStampKeylessTemplateTests requires 3 CognitiveServices accounts with local auth off and passes; ControlPlane.Tests, ArchTests and BFF unit tests have no new failures; catalog -Verify passes; bicep-e2e-dry-run PASS.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (both sides from short paths, same file count, Compress-Archive) and the CVE check are recorded in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every escalation trigger is answered in the notes (fired or not, with evidence); demo's follow-on is recorded on T242c.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-10-06 (session 38). Implementation commit 514a4638e. Template + code only — no live Azure change
    (T186 deploys a stamp; T230 makes the stamp-side MI call).

    FACTS (read-only, 2026-10-06): no `spaarke-contentsafety-dev` account exists (dev subscription Cognitive Services
    accounts: spaarke-openai-dev [AIServices, eastus] + one unrelated). Dev BFF sets AiSafety__ContentSafety__Endpoint
    = https://spaarke-openai-dev.cognitiveservices.azure.com/ (MI on) — unaffected. Demo BFF (Stopped, Production) has
    no AiSafety setting → recorded on T242c + config/spaarke-resources.yaml. sprksharedprod-api Stopped/retired. Key
    Vault spaarke-spekvcert holds no ContentSafety secret (live or soft-deleted).

    DONE: content-safety.bicep keyless (disableLocalAuth true, custom subdomain, listKeys output removed) + Cognitive
    Services User for the stamp UAMI; customer.bicep wires it (name sprk-{customer}-{env}-contentsafety, S0),
    AiSafety__ContentSafety__Endpoint app setting, LOAD-BEARING output contentSafetyEndpoint. L2 chain copied from
    T242 redisEndpoint: ArmDeploymentRunner.MapOutputs → BicepDeployOutputs.ContentSafetyEndpoint (required) → H2a
    check + InterStepState.ContentSafetyEndpoint → PerEnvSourceCatalog from-h2a-output:content_safety_endpoint
    (+ generator allow-list) → HandlerRunInputs H4b → manifest per_env_settings AiSafety__ContentSafety__Endpoint.
    ContentSafety-ApiKey removed from the manifest (generated/* regenerated, -Verify OK) and from PinnedManifestGaps.
    BFF AiSafetyModule: hard-coded dev fallback removed; endpoint required outside Development/Testing (startup
    InvalidOperationException naming AiSafetyModule + the exempt environments); Development/Testing unset → no base
    address → scans fail open via the services' existing catch; non-https rejected. Verify-ContentSafetyResource.ps1
    keyless (Entra token) — RUN against dev: Prompt Shields 200, Groundedness 200 (eastus). Keyless ArchTest
    CognitiveServices minimum 2 → 3.

    DEVIATION (region, recorded): the POML constraint said contentSafetyLocation defaults to the stamp location. The
    Microsoft region table (learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/content-safety/region-availability, updated
    2026-09-18) shows westus2 — the stamp default — has Prompt Shields but NO Groundedness Detection (US regions with
    both: westus, eastus, eastus2, canadaeast). Following the stamp location would have made every groundedness check
    fail open silently, so contentSafetyLocation defaults to westus (nearest to westus2), split-region like
    openAiLocation. The module header's old "West US 2 required" note was wrong.

    ADDED FROM REVIEW: ArmTemplateInspector rule R4 — H2a rejects, Resumable and before any ARM call
    (template-outputs-missing), a resolved template that does not declare every output H2a requires
    (ArmDeploymentRunner.RequiredOutputNames, pinned to MapOutputs by a source-scan test). Covers T242's redisEndpoint
    too. Behavioural test: Testing + no endpoint → PromptShieldService.ScanAsync returns FailedOpen.

    VERIFIED: ControlPlane.Tests 2122 passed / 0 failed / 1 skipped; ArchTests 363/363; BFF unit 14327 passed / 0
    failed / 54 skipped (full run) + safety subset 84/0/1 after the last edits; catalog -Verify OK; customer.json =
    fresh compile (semantic); bicep-e2e-dry-run Build PASS (8 warnings, all pre-existing lines). BFF §10: publish
    Release, Compress-Archive Optimal, fresh short-path worktrees — master 23bdc5679 = 48,108,908 bytes (45.88 MB, 214
    files) vs branch 514a4638e = 48,109,097 bytes (45.88 MB, 214 files): +189 bytes (~0.00 MB). CVE: `dotnet list
    package --vulnerable --include-transitive` → no vulnerable packages; no package changes. Placement: design.md §17
    T246 entry (existing module, no new surface).

    ESCALATION TRIGGERS: (1) no other component needs a Content Safety key or endpoint — consumers are only
    PromptShieldService + GroundednessCheckService via the named client (not fired). (2) kind ContentSafety accepts
    disableLocalAuth + custom subdomain at 2024-10-01 (compiles; same API as openai.bicep) (not fired). (3) no test host
    or deployed environment other than demo lacks the endpoint (dev sets it; shared-prod retired) (not fired; demo → T242c).

    STEP 9.5: adr-check — V1 (exception message must name the exempt environments) FIXED; W2 placement FIXED (design.md
    §17); W3 ValidateOnStart/options class — accepted, follows the T242 CacheModule startup-check precedent (throws at
    host build); W4 Content Safety added to T230's MI-call list; W5 D13 "no flag day" vs boot check — governed by D22 +
    plan row ("fail at boot when unset"), demo follow-on on T242c; W6 design.md/guide D-12 wording FIXED; W7 test
    placement mirrors CacheModuleTests; W8 pre-T246 stamps keep a dead ApiKey KV ref — none exist; D-12 "shareable" is
    permitted-not-required (no conflict; S0 has no fixed fee). code-review — 0 Critical; W1 FIXED (R4); W2 recorded
    below; W3 FIXED (region default); W4 FIXED; W5 FIXED (script stderr/exit codes); W6 FIXED (justification); S1
    FIXED; S2 kept (asserts the called URL); S7 FIXED (registry content_safety_endpoint; dev OpenAI region eastus).

    FOLLOW-UPS (not T186 blockers unless noted): (a) worker upgrade with a run in flight whose H2a completed under the
    old worker → H4b PerEnvInputMissing that resume cannot heal (re-run or patch InterStepState) — deploy the worker
    with no run in flight (same for T242); (b) H2a's global-name pre-check does not cover Cognitive Services custom
    subdomains (openai/docintel/contentsafety) — a collision quarantines mid-deploy; (c) Decommission-Customer.ps1 does
    not purge soft-deleted Cognitive Services accounts (re-provisioning the same customerId/env fails until retention
    ends); (d) H0 preflight could check the Content Safety region offers Groundedness; (e) upgrade runs of pre-T246
    stamps would see the new app setting as what-if drift (no such stamps exist); (f) doc drift found: the retired dev
    app `spe-api-dev-67e2xz` is still named in ~40 docs/skills (it no longer exists; dev BFF is spaarke-bff-dev).
  </notes>
